\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Terms to understand: \par
\line nucleotide \endash  in this context, one of the four individual blocks (ACGT)\line point mutation - a single nucleotide base in a DNA or RNA sequence is changed, added, or removed.\line homologous DNA strand \endash  same sequence of genes as another strand in the same order, but the alleles are different. \line  - the \lquote slot\rquote  for the gene is in the same spot on both strands, but the actual nucleotide (ACGT) can be different \line\line Hamming distance - a measure of the minimum number of point mutations that could have occurred on the evolutionary path between the two strands.\line  - rule: this distance is only defined for sequences of equal length. If you have two sequences of unequal length, you should compute the Hamming distance over the shorter length.\line\line E: \line{\pict{\*\picprop{\sp{\sn wzDescription}{\sv Image}}{\sp{\sn posv}{\sv 1}}
